WEBVTT

00:03.960 --> 00:06.880
So now let's have a quick comparison between tables and views.

00:06.920 --> 00:10.400
Tables stores the actual data physically at a database.

00:10.400 --> 00:14.560
So the tables where the data is persisted with in the other hand the views.

00:14.600 --> 00:16.000
They are virtual tables.

00:16.000 --> 00:22.080
And they do not store any data inside the database, but they present the data from the underlying tables.

00:22.080 --> 00:25.600
So that means views don't persist any data physically.

00:25.600 --> 00:29.200
Now the tables are hard to maintain and as well hard to change.

00:29.200 --> 00:33.280
So it needs a lot of efforts in order to do any change, like adding columns.

00:33.280 --> 00:38.640
And moving columns always requires a lot of efforts for the migration, especially if you have large

00:38.640 --> 00:39.200
tables.

00:39.200 --> 00:44.880
But in the other hand, the views are way easier to maintain and very flexible to change.

00:44.880 --> 00:48.200
All that you have to do is only to change the query of the view.

00:48.200 --> 00:52.480
So that means you can very quickly change stuff in the views compared to the tables.

00:52.480 --> 00:56.480
But if you are talking about performance, tables are faster than views.

00:56.480 --> 01:01.400
For example, if you go and do a simple select on the table, you will get the data back as soon as

01:01.440 --> 01:03.040
the database fetches the data.

01:03.040 --> 01:08.600
But if you are selecting something from the view, it is actually two queries the query that comes from

01:08.600 --> 01:12.600
the user and as well the second query is the view query.

01:12.600 --> 01:18.160
And the query of the view could be very complicated in order to extract the data from the underlying

01:18.200 --> 01:18.760
table.

01:18.760 --> 01:23.680
So selecting something from the view is always slower than selecting something from a table.

01:23.720 --> 01:26.040
Now, if you have a table you can read from a table.

01:26.040 --> 01:28.080
And as well you can write to a table.

01:28.120 --> 01:32.080
But the views are read only as the name says, it is only a view.

01:32.120 --> 01:35.160
You cannot go and write something to the database using the view.

01:35.200 --> 01:39.320
Okay, so those are the big differences between views and tables.
